; WaveSmithDrawers -- the installed drawers on Workbench, on ANY machine:
; WaveSmithInstall needs W=rtg32 (its Installer clicks are measured
; there), so this copies the package's Files into SYS:Tools the way the
; Installer does for a novice -- the drawer whole, the GlowIcon set
; (Files/Icons/Glow/WaveSmith) over its classic icons, the drawer's
; GlowIcon beside it -- and
; DEV:Test/WSDrawers.rexx opens SYS:Tools and every drawer, grabbing the
; screen after each (arranged-glow-<n>.ppm); then the classic icons, as
; the Installer copies them when they are chosen (arranged-classic-<n>).
; The layout itself: tools/arrange_drawers.py. Mostly for W=pal, the
; tightest Workbench (640x256, Topaz 8).
;   gmake autotest T=WaveSmithDrawers W=pal LIMIT=180
FailAt 21
Wait 10
If NOT EXISTS DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Install
  Echo >DEV:Test/auto.log "SKIPPED: no DEV:Release (gmake release-drawer)"
  Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
  Quit
EndIf
Delete >NIL: SYS:Tools/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info DEV:Test/arranged-#? ALL QUIET
Echo >DEV:Test/auto.log "WaveSmithDrawers"
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith ALL CLONE QUIET
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/Icons/Glow/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith ALL CLONE QUIET
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/Icons/Glow/WaveSmithDrawer.info SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info CLONE QUIET
List >>DEV:Test/auto.log SYS:Tools/WaveSmith ALL FILES LFORMAT "  %P%N %L"
RX DEV:Test/WSDrawers.rexx glow
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith ALL CLONE QUIET
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/WaveSmith.info SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info CLONE QUIET
RX DEV:Test/WSDrawers.rexx classic
Delete >NIL: SYS:Tools/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info ALL QUIET
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
